  "rule": "OpenStreetMap is the base: every building of our own OSM extract is kept unchanged. An Overture building is added only if none of its sources is OpenStreetMap and (1) it does not overlap our OSM extract or an addition already accepted: dropped if its centroid is inside an OSM footprint, an OSM centroid is inside it, or the outlines intersect at all (outer rings); (2) it is plausible: at least 25 m2, confidence at least 0.7 where the source gives one, not above 5000 m2 unless its confidence is at least 0.8, and at least 4 m wide (short side of its smallest enclosing rectangle; containers, trailers and vehicles are narrower); (3) its centroid is on land inside a municipio; (4) it is not a small footprint (under 60 m2) whose outline comes within 1.5 m of an OSM footprint (taken as part of the mapped building). Tests run in that order and a candidate is counted under the first one it fails. Added records have bit 7 (0x80) of kind set; kind is house under 400 m2, otherwise other; height is the source's own or 0.",
